
  Average Directional Index (ADX)
  ================================

 Pure Strength Indicator
 
 It provides Trend Strength and covers false breakouts detected from MACD and RSI. RSI can be fooled by persistent over-bought/over-sold conditions

 ------ "25" --------
 
 ADX is pure strength on a scale of 0-100. Anything above 25 needs to be taken seriously. Below can be considered low strength


When to Use ADX Over MACD & RSI:
=================================
If you need to confirm whether a trend is strong enough to trade (ADX > 25) rather than just detecting a crossover.

If you want to avoid false signals in choppy markets, where MACD and RSI alone may mislead.

